      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- average enrollment: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- enrollment variance: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- subjects offered: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- degree-granting courses: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- Political Science: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- Chemistry: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- Biology: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- subject count: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- minimum term start date: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_START_DATE\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"Political Science\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Political Science'\"\n- \"biology and chemistry department\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME IN ('Chemistry', 'Biology')\"\n- \"Course 17\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '17'\"\n- \"Course 5\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n- \"Course 7\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Biology'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, what is the average and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, considering only subjects with more than 0 enrolled students and courses that are degree-granting, and only include departments that are not 'Political Science' (Course 17)?\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrollment_variance FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT WHERE tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '17' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY enrollment_variance DESC;\n```\n2. For each department and academic year where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 0, and the department is either Chemistry or Biology, provide the count of subjects and the minimum start date of the term.\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME AS department, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR AS academic_year, COUNT(DISTINCT tso.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, MIN(ata.TERM_START_DATE) AS min_term_start_date FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ata ON tso.TERM_CODE = ata.TERM_CODE WHERE tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME IN ('Chemistry', 'Biology') GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department, what is the average and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 enrolled students, degree-granting courses, and excluding departments that are 'Political Science' (Course 17)), and for Chemistry and Biology departments and each academic year where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 0, what is the count of subjects and the minimum start date of the term? Present the department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, academic year, subject count, and minimum term start date in that order. Do not return any rounded answers."
